  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a string `s`, partition the string into one or more **substrings** such that the characters in each substring are **unique**. That is, no letter appears in a single substring more than **once**.\n\nOutput *the **smallest** number of substrings in such a partition.*\n\nKeep in mind that each character should belong to exactly one substring in a partition.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"abacaba\"\nOutput: 4\nExplanation:\nTwo possible partitions are (\"a\",\"ba\",\"cab\",\"a\") and (\"ab\",\"a\",\"ca\",\"ba\").\nIt can be shown that 4 is the minimum number of substrings needed.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"ssssss\"\nOutput: 6\nExplanation:\nThe only valid partition is (\"s\",\"s\",\"s\",\"s\",\"s\",\"s\").\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 105`\n* `s` is composed of only English lowercase letters.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
